# Files that are fine to keep in git but shouldn't ship in the published
# package archive.
#
# .pubignore follows .gitignore syntax; unlike .gitignore, listing a file
# here does NOT hide it from git, only from `dart pub publish`. Note:
# creating this file means `dart pub publish` stops also deferring to
# .gitignore automatically — so this list is written to stand on its own
# (build artifacts and editor files included), not just as additions.

# Build/tool artifacts — should never be tracked, but listed explicitly
# since .pubignore's presence means .gitignore is no longer consulted too.
build/
example/build/
.dart_tool/
example/.dart_tool/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store

# Libraries shouldn't ship their own lockfile — consumers resolve their own.
/pubspec.lock

# Maintainer-only docs/tooling — irrelevant to package consumers.
PUBLISHING.md
Makefile

# The example app's native runner scaffolding (Gradle/Xcode projects, app
# icons, plists, ...) — pub.dev only needs example/lib, example/pubspec.yaml,
# and example/test to demonstrate real usage; the platform projects are
# noise on the package page and don't affect `flutter run` from within
# example/ (Flutter regenerates them from `flutter create .` if ever
# needed).
example/android/
example/ios/
